   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Causing an action",
     "texto": [
      "The causative presents someone as the one who makes another person or thing carry out an action. Some common forms take **-이-, -히-, -리-, -기-, -우-, -구-** or **-추-**: 먹다 → **먹이다** (to feed), 입다 → **입히다** (to dress someone), 자다 → **재우다** (to put someone to sleep), 웃다 → **웃기다** (to make someone laugh). There is no safe rule for choosing the suffix: learn each verb with its causative form.",
      "아기에게 우유를 **먹여요** = I give milk to the baby."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Use and conjugation",
     "texto": [
      "They conjugate like normal verbs: 먹이다 → **먹여요**, 입히다 → **입혀요**, 재우다 → **재워요**. Some forms coincide with passives: the meaning and the arguments of the sentence let you tell them apart."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
